WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:18.760
My name is Natalija Vladisavljević.

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:26.280
I am working in the field of dance choreography,

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:28.280
writing for dance,

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:31.800
leading workshops.
As a choreographer,

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:35.640
I find inspiration in my head.

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:41.840
I’m inspired by the space,
the people, the stage...&nbsp;

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:47.240
A choreographer thinks
about what she'll write,

00:00:47.240 --> 00:00:51.840
which means that when I get inspired
to write something about myself,

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:57.440
I must consider what is it I want to
write about, what am I thinking about,

00:00:57.680 --> 00:01:03.960
and only then do I start
gathering information

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:06.560
and actions on the stage.

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:12.640
That's how a choreographer
works on how to organise herself.

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:17.880
For my new show called
Dance in the 21st Century,

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:21.520
I’m working with my dancers

00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:27.240
on choreographic, graphical,
and music scores,

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:31.680
for the instructions of contemporary dance.

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:39.120
When I write the scores,
I imagine what my show would look like.

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:45.280
I think about many different topics
and choreographic segments.

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:51.880
And once I put it all together
and wrap it up, the show is ready.

00:01:51.880 --> 00:01:59.960
As a choreographer, I think about the lights,
costumes, space, dramaturgy.

00:01:59.960 --> 00:02:10.080
Besides being a choreographer,
I also&nbsp;lead contemporary dance workshops.

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:13.960
I sometimes write very precise instructions,

00:02:13.960 --> 00:02:19.200
and sometimes I ask them to work
through improvisation, the way they like.

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:25.360
I need to see their choreographies
at the end of the workshop,

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:27.680
and then we talk about them.

00:02:35.440 --> 00:02:39.480
Witch Dance (Hexentanz) 
is a contemporary dance

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:47.080
with a lot of elements for movements 

00:02:48.280 --> 00:02:57.320
and I imagine myself in a way that I can,
with my own body,

00:02:57.320 --> 00:03:02.480
initiate my own dance
and that is the way to maintain my strength.

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:12.520
Well, I chose Hexentanz, "The Witch Dance",

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:18.040
because it was important for me

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:21.880
to work in this contemporary dance,

00:03:21.880 --> 00:03:24.480
like Mary Wigman.

00:03:25.240 --> 00:03:28.560
And I chose that one

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:36.160
because Mary Wigman and I
have the same facial expression.

00:03:36.160 --> 00:03:39.320
Yes, I wrote a libretto,

00:03:39.320 --> 00:03:44.680
and I wrote it down as I imagined it,

00:03:44.680 --> 00:03:47.880
I imagined how it would look.

00:03:48.840 --> 00:03:52.040
So, I started

00:03:52.920 --> 00:03:55.800
imagining, imagining, imagining...

00:03:55.800 --> 00:03:59.480
And I wrote that story.

